Error [jet.MoveWithoutMarker]: `.push()` takes `item`, but `item` is used again later
  --> tests/ui/ownership/read_param_into_owning_argument_matches_across_call_forms.jet:23:15
    |
 23 |     rows.push(item)
    |               ^^^^
  --> tests/ui/ownership/read_param_into_owning_argument_matches_across_call_forms.jet:24:18
    |
 24 |     rows.len() + item.len()
    |                  ^^^^ `item` is used again here
 Why: `.push()` takes ownership of this argument, and a call never copies on its own, so `item` has no value after this call
 Fix: Write `item.copy()` to pass a copy and keep `item`, or reorder so this call is the last use of `item`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0209

